  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to interact with HPAC through a series of molecular pathways involving the P2X purinoceptor 1, TE-9, and LB2241-RCC. These targets are all engaged by the same compound, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which suggests a common mechanism of action. The evidence indicates that Mollicellin N may act as a modulator of the P2X receptor family, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways that ultimately lead to interactions with HPAC. The consistent presence of this compound as a target of multiple entities, coupled with the shared interaction with HPAC, suggests a possible role in the regulation of cellular processes involving the P2X receptors. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to influence cellular functions through these molecular targets, offering a plausible mechanism for its interaction with HPAC.",
